From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 19:39:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] OHOS: sign the downloaded native package-manager binary.
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The platform-cfg patch (0001) only gets the *right* platform package
downloaded — confirmed on real hardware that OHOS's exec() signature
check still EACCESs the freshly-downloaded musl binary (unrelated to
the unix mode bit set right after the rename; this device enforces
code-signing on every exec regardless of ELF/libc correctness — the
container this bottle is built in does not enforce it, so this branch
would in principle be a no-op there). Sign in place right after the
existing chmod; deliberately not probing the binary here (executing an
unknown freshly-downloaded exe from inside the build turned out to be
its own source of container failures) — the settle delay between
signing and it being runnable is covered by the caller's own retry
loop (`vp_with_retry` in the formula's test block, and any real
invocation of `vp create`/`vp install`). Both download_*_package_manager
functions share this exact block verbatim.

Uses `selfsign` (ohos-bst-light), not the SDK's `binary-sign-tool`:
verified on real hardware and in the OHOS CI container that
binary-sign-tool corrupts this binary's ELF structure outright — a
binary-sign-tool-signed copy of @pnpm/exe.linux-arm64-musl SIGSEGVs
immediately on exec, even in the container, which doesn't enforce
signatures at all (so this isn't a permission/signature-check failure,
the file itself is broken). ohos-bst-light's selfsign preserves the
ELF and the binary runs fine afterward. Same static-ELF class of bug
as bun and CGO_ENABLED=0 Go binaries — see the tap's binary-sign-tool
notes.
---
 crates/vite_pm_cli/src/package_manager.rs | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/crates/vite_pm_cli/src/package_manager.rs b/crates/vite_pm_cli/src/package_manager.rs
index 62c7c95..e32e9d5 100644
--- a/crates/vite_pm_cli/src/package_manager.rs
+++ b/crates/vite_pm_cli/src/package_manager.rs
@@ -1053,6 +1053,17 @@ async fn download_bun_package_manager(
         use std::os::unix::fs::PermissionsExt;
         tokio::fs::set_permissions(&native_bin_dest, fs::Permissions::from_mode(0o755)).await?;
     }
+    #[cfg(target_env = "ohos")]
+    {
+        let _ = std::process::Command::new("selfsign")
+            .arg(&native_bin_dest)
+            .status();
+        use std::os::unix::fs::PermissionsExt;
+        let _ = std::fs::set_permissions(
+            &native_bin_dest,
+            std::fs::Permissions::from_mode(0o755),
+        );
+    }

     // Clean up the extracted package directory
     remove_dir_all_force(&package_dir).await?;
@@ -1239,6 +1250,17 @@ async fn download_pnpm_native_package_manager(
         use std::os::unix::fs::PermissionsExt;
         tokio::fs::set_permissions(&native_bin_dest, fs::Permissions::from_mode(0o755)).await?;
     }
+    #[cfg(target_env = "ohos")]
+    {
+        let _ = std::process::Command::new("selfsign")
+            .arg(&native_bin_dest)
+            .status();
+        use std::os::unix::fs::PermissionsExt;
+        let _ = std::fs::set_permissions(
+            &native_bin_dest,
+            std::fs::Permissions::from_mode(0o755),
+        );
+    }

     // Clean up the extracted package directory
     remove_dir_all_force(&package_dir).await?;
